Smallframe third-party dependency notes
Reviewed: 2026-09-17

Scope
-----
The root Apache-2.0 license applies to Smallframe's original work, not to
third-party dependencies. This review inspected package-lock.json license
fields, cargo metadata --locked for the locked Rust graph, tracked source
notices and Git authorship. It is a metadata/source-notice review, not an
independent legal opinion or proof of ownership of every contribution.

No vendored third-party binaries were found among tracked repository files.
Generated artifacts, installed dependencies and downloaded toolchains are
excluded from Git and may contain third-party code and required notices.

JavaScript and local tooling
----------------------------
The npm lockfile declares MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, 0BSD, CC0-1.0
and combinations including LGPL-3.0-or-later. No dependency entry with a
node_modules path lacked a license field at review time.

The LGPL entries are the sharp/libvips platform packages brought in by
Miniflare, directly and through Wrangler. They are local development/tooling
dependencies, not Smallframe app-package dependencies. Their upstream license
terms remain applicable if those binaries or a development environment
containing them are redistributed. Apache-2.0 does not replace LGPL terms.

Runtime/build dependencies such as Lit (BSD-3-Clause), @noble/ed25519 (MIT),
canonicalize (Apache-2.0), and Automerge (MIT, Rust crate) retain their
upstream notices. Review the actual generated browser/CLI artifacts before
any binary release; this file is not a complete bundled-license collection.

Rust
----
The locked Rust dependency graph declares permissive licenses or permissive
alternatives: principally MIT/Apache-2.0, plus BSD variants, Unicode-3.0,
Zlib, BSL-1.0, MIT-0 and Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception alternatives.
The r-efi entries offer MIT OR Apache-2.0 OR LGPL-2.1-or-later; LGPL is not
the only available choice. Preserve the notices for the selected licenses,
including Unicode data and any applicable exceptions.

Release work still required
---------------------------
For each distributed browser bundle, Wasm module, CLI binary or tool image:
identify the components actually included; collect their full licenses,
copyright and NOTICE texts; satisfy source/relinking requirements where
applicable; and carry these materials in the distribution. The existing
scripts/generate-sbom.mjs inventories npm metadata only and does not replace
that artifact-specific work or cover the Rust graph.

Recheck when dependency versions or distribution formats change. No binary
release, deployment or independent compliance certification is implied by
this source-license change.
